# Patterns use **/ so they match at any depth (Docker, unlike gitignore, does not match
# bare names against nested paths). Stale **/*.tsbuildinfo in particular must be excluded, or
# `tsc --composite` treats the build as up to date and emits nothing.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.dockerignore

**/.expo/
.claude/
*.har
docs/private/

# The rest mirrors .gcloudignore. Real deploys go through `gcloud run deploy --source .`, which
# strips these before Docker ever sees them; without them here, a *local* `docker build` sends
# the whole 30+ GB corpus as build context and never finishes.
#
# Benchmark data: cached Open-Meteo responses and HTML reports, never needed in the build.
data/

# Photo originals at the repo root — the pages serve the resized copies in
# packages/server/public, so the multi-megabyte source files never need copying.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# Secrets and the deployment target, both read outside the build.
.env
deploy.env

# Native build output under the mobile package: regenerable, and ~1 GB of iOS Pods/build.
packages/mobile/ios/
packages/mobile/android/
